Kickstart the watchdog in the initramfs

The initramfs can wedge trying to mount a corrupted rootfs, which leaves the
board hanging forever instead of falling back to a bootable slot. Start the
hardware watchdog as soon as the driver is loaded so an unmountable rootfs
resets the device into the recovery chain.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded specific]

--- a/init-boot.sh	2025-03-25 12:29:30.049843574 +0100
+++ b/init-boot.sh	2025-03-25 12:29:21.393169964 +0100
@@ -12,6 +12,12 @@
 
 modprobe -v nvme
 
+# Start the watchdog immediately
+# If a bad rootfs update is installed, the initramfs will get
+# stuck trying to mount a corrupted partition.
+echo "Kicking the watchdog..."
+echo >/dev/watchdog || true
+
 rootdev=""
 opt="rw"
 wait=""
